<p>Why do so many people think online platforms have been good for democracy? Part of the answer may be that these platforms give people a voice at time when <a href="https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2024/02/28/views-about-political-representation/">many feel voiceless</a>. A median of 60% in the 37 countries surveyed say access to the internet and social media has increased people’s ability to have a meaningful voice in politics.</p>



<p>And access to the internet and social media can inform people about current events: A median of 77% think it has led people to be more informed.</p>



<p>At the same time, people are certainly aware of social media’s pernicious effects. A median of 79% believe it has made it easier to manipulate people with false information and 68% say it has made people more divided in their political opinions.</p>


