<p>The survey also finds that the social media platforms people use vary across the globe, although Facebook tends to be the most common among the five we asked about, followed by Instagram. Many – especially young people – also say they use TikTok, while fewer overall use X (formerly known as Twitter) or Snapchat.</p>



<p><em>For more, read “<a href="https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2026/10/01/social-media-platform-use-around-the-world/" data-type="link" data-id="https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2026/10/01/social-media-platform-use-around-the-world/">Social Media Platform Use Around the World</a>.”</em></p>



<p>For this report, we surveyed 45,658 people in 37 countries from Feb. 8 to May 13, 2026. Additional data on Americans’ social media platform use comes from a survey of 5,511 adults conducted from Jan. 30 to June 18, 2026.</p>



